WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.691
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, November eleventh.

2
00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:12.380
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.855
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:30.477
Today: hundreds of schools in Italy evacuated after a bomb alert, a U.S. soldier arrested in Britain on suspicion of spying for Russia, drone shelter alerts across the Baltic states, two storms hitting Portugal, and border clashes between Ethiopia and Eritrea.

5
00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:31.906
We start with Italy.

6
00:00:31.906 --> 00:00:43.171
Reuters reports that at least three hundred schools in Italy were evacuated this morning after receiving the same bomb alert message, according to the education minister.

7
00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:44.341
Next, the United Kingdom.

8
00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:49.275
The Record reports British authorities said a U.S.

9
00:00:49.275 --> 00:00:53.895
Army member was arrested on suspicion of spying for Russia, and BNO News reports the FBI confirmed the arrest.

10
00:00:53.895 --> 00:00:56.157
Separately, Reuters reports the U.S.

11
00:00:56.157 --> 00:01:05.326
Justice Department says an Iran backed militant helped plot an attack on R A F Fairford in England while he was held in a U.S. jail.

12
00:01:05.326 --> 00:01:06.415
Turning to the Baltic states.

13
00:01:06.415 --> 00:01:17.914
Reuters reports Lithuania, Latvia and Estonia issued a flurry of alerts urging people to seek shelter from unidentified drones entering from Russia or Belarus, then withdrew them, officials and media said.

14
00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:24.689
Reuters also reports Latvia and Lithuania have warned of new drone threats, as Finland adopts new curbs.

15
00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:25.827
In Portugal.

16
00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:44.655
The State Department's travel service says Storm Bruna is bringing rain, strong winds and rough seas to mainland Portugal through Friday, and a second storm, Charles, is expected to reach the mainland today with heavy rain, winds of up to one hundred forty kilometers per hour, and a risk of river overflows and flash flooding.

17
00:01:44.655 --> 00:01:50.568
Britain's Foreign Office has also updated its Portugal travel advice with information on severe weather.

18
00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:52.771
And in Ethiopia and Eritrea.

19
00:01:52.771 --> 00:02:07.251
The Critical Threats Project says several conflict trackers reported clashes between Ethiopian and Eritrean forces near the Eritrean border town of Badme on Monday, November ninth, though it could not confirm which side of the border the fighting took place on.

20
00:02:07.251 --> 00:02:13.713
It assesses that the military buildup and clashes are likely becoming a sustained, low intensity border war.

21
00:02:13.713 --> 00:02:16.871
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:02:16.871 --> 00:02:23.314
In Europe, Reuters reports a drone attack left part of the Ukrainian city of Kryvyi Rih without power.

23
00:02:23.314 --> 00:02:36.972
In the Middle East, Reuters reports an Israeli airstrike on a metal foundry in Gaza City killed three people, and four more people, including a thirteen year old, were killed in other parts of Gaza City and in Khan Younis, medics said.

24
00:02:36.972 --> 00:02:52.052
In South Asia, Pakistan's Tribal News Network reports militants opened fire from the surrounding mountains on police in the Ghambat area of Kohat district, in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, this morning, as officers headed out for an operation against illegal mines.

25
00:02:52.052 --> 00:03:00.061
In Africa, BBC Africa reports a military court in the Democratic Republic of the Congo has sentenced sixty six soldiers to death for cowardice.

26
00:03:00.061 --> 00:03:08.866
And the Long War Journal reports Ugandan troops have begun withdrawing from Somalia, and U.S. forces have left a key base there.

27
00:03:08.866 --> 00:03:18.517
In the Americas, the U.N. humanitarian office says armed violence in Arcahaie and Cabaret, in Haiti, has displaced more than five thousand nine hundred people since late October.

28
00:03:18.517 --> 00:03:27.935
The Miami Herald reports Haitian police and Salvadoran troops destroyed the house of the leader of the 400 Mawozo gang in Croix des Bouquets on Sunday, November eighth.

29
00:03:27.935 --> 00:03:41.217
And in cyber, The Record reports Russian state linked hackers compromised government email servers in Romania and Kazakhstan to secretly intercept messages with NATO and European Union officials, according to new research.

30
00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:54.960
Microsoft says it is tracking a Brazil focused threat cluster it calls Storm thirty three fifty, mainly affecting financial services, payments, banking and digital assets, as well as healthcare, transportation and logistics.

31
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.384
That's today's brief.

32
00:03:56.384 --> 00:04:04.572
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

33
00:04:04.572 --> 00:04:13.139
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

34
00:04:13.139 --> 00:04:15.308
This brief is digitally narrated.

35
00:04:15.308 --> 00:04:16.278
Questions?

36
00:04:16.278 --> 00:04:19.821
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

37
00:04:19.821 --> 00:04:21.827
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
